>> title: Pizzelle
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: anise, italian, waffle iron, teatime, christmas
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: pizelle, ferratelle, cancelle, Italian waffle cookies, anise waffle cookies
>> servings: 30
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — forty-five seconds in a hot iron and there is no looking at them while they cook: pale ones are soft and never crisp, dark ones are bitter, and they have to be shaped or flattened within a few seconds of coming off because they set hard as they cool
>> step.6: press in the hot iron for 45 sec

Heat a #pizzelle iron{}.

Beat @eggs{3%large}(150 g) with @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g).

Whisk @melted butter{1/2%cup}(113 g; cooled), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL), and @anise extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) into @&(~1)egg mixture{}.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{1 3/4%cup}(220 g), @baking powder{2%tsp}(9.6 g), and @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g).

Stir @&(~1)dry ingredients{} into @&(~2)batter{}.

Press @&(~1)batter{} in rounded tablespoons in the iron for ~{45%sec}.
